Unable to determine UFFD GC flag because the kernel version is not available and
PRODUCT_ENABLE_UFFD_GC is "default".
You can fix this by:
  1. [Recommended] Making the kernel version available.
    (1). Set PRODUCT_OTA_ENFORCE_VINTF_KERNEL_REQUIREMENTS to "true".
    (2). If you are still getting this message after doing so, see the warning about
         PRODUCT_OTA_ENFORCE_VINTF_KERNEL_REQUIREMENTS in the build logs.
  or
  2. Explicitly setting PRODUCT_ENABLE_UFFD_GC to "true" or "false" based on the kernel version.
    (1). Set PRODUCT_ENABLE_UFFD_GC to "true" if the kernel is a GKI kernel and is android12-5.4
         or above, or a non-GKI kernel that supports userfaultfd(2) and MREMAP_DONTUNMAP.
    (2). Set PRODUCT_ENABLE_UFFD_GC to "false" otherwise.
